The most common cause is that the **parent re-renders**, which re-renders all children by default—even with identical props. Here are the typical culprits:

**1. Inline object/array props (most common)**
```jsx
// ❌ Creates a new object every render
<Child data={{name: "Alice"}} />

// ✅ Create once outside the component
const data = {name: "Alice"};
<Child data={data} />
```

**2. Inline function props**
```jsx
// ❌ New function every render
<Child onClick={() => console.log("clicked")} />

// ✅ Use useCallback to memoize
const handleClick = useCallback(() => console.log("clicked"), []);
<Child onClick={handleClick} />
```

**3. Child not memoized**
```jsx
// ❌ Always re-renders when parent re-renders
export function Child({name}) {
  return <div>{name}</div>;
}

// ✅ Skip re-render if props are the same
export const Child = React.memo(({name}) => {
  return <div>{name}</div>;
});
```

**To debug**, add a log to your child component:
```jsx
export const Child = React.memo(({name}) => {
  console.log("Child rendered with props:", name);
  return <div>{name}</div>;
});
```

If you see the log every time even though the `name` value doesn't change, one of the above is the issue. Share your code if you need help pinpointing it.
